# Slack MCP policy

Slack MCP access is **read-only by default**.

## Allowed without asking
- Reading channels, threads, messages, users, and related Slack metadata via MCP

## Forbidden unless Kirk explicitly permits it in this conversation
- Posting, sending, or replying to messages
- Editing or deleting messages
- Creating, renaming, archiving, or otherwise modifying channels
- Adding/removing reactions, pins, bookmarks, or similar write actions
- Inviting/removing users, changing topic/purpose, or any other mutating Slack API/MCP call

If a task seems to require a Slack write, **stop and ask Kirk for explicit permission** first. Do not treat earlier permission in another chat/work area as consent here.
